{
 "version": 1,
 "title": "Polysynth Brass",
 "category": "80s and synth-pop leads",
 "text": "Sound: the big, bright synth brass of 80s pop and rock: chords that swell slightly into each hit, the filter opening with a 'blare', wide with chorus.\n\nHow it's built: two saws a few cents apart through the Ladder filter; the filter envelope has a short ATTACK (60 ms) so the brightness swells in like a brass player's breath, then settles; the VCA's envelope is softer at the start too. Chorus (II) and some Reverb. Six voices.\n\nPlay: chords, punchy and held; brass riffs.\n\nTweak: the filter envelope's ATTACK (slower is more brass-like, shorter more of a stab), its SUSTAIN, the filter's CV.",
